.TH HMAP_FREE_DATA 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
hmap_free_data \- Free the data associated with a tuple in a hash map

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/hmap_internal.h>

.IB int
.IB hmap_free_data(TUPLE* tuple);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBhmap_free_data\fR function frees the data associated with a tuple in a hash map. It takes a pointer to the tuple as an argument.

The function takes the following parameter:
.IB TUPLE*
A pointer to the tuple whose data needs to be freed.

The function returns an integer indicating the result of the operation. Possible return values include:
.IB HMAP_SUCCESS
The data was successfully freed.
.IB HMAP_DATA_TYPE_INVALID
The data type of the tuple is invalid.

The \fBhmap_free_data\fR function is intended to be used to free the data associated with a tuple in a hash map to avoid memory leaks.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBhmap_free_data\fR function to free the data associated with a tuple in a hash map:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/hmap_internal.h>

int main() {
    HMAP_DB* hmap_db;
    // Initialize the hash map database
    hmap_init(&hmap_db);

    // Add a tuple with a string data type
    TUPLE* tuple = hmap_add_tuple_with_data(&hmap_db, "example1", 8, "data1");

    // Free the data associated with the tuple
    int result = hmap_free_data(tuple);

    if(result == HMAP_SUCCESS) {
        printf("Data freed successfully\n");
    } else {
        printf("Failed to free data\n");
    }

    // Free the hash map database
    hmap_destroy(&hmap_db);

    return 0;
}
.nef